 ## Overview
-3D Table Animation is a method for controlling the movement and shape of volumetric gases by storing control values in a 3D table surrounding the gas volume in world space [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of directing gas flow by interpolating values from lattice points to determine sample-specific control parameters. It is distinguished from its parent method, [3D Table Computation on GPU](2083-3d-table-computation-on-gpu.md), by its specific application to gas animation via functional flow fields and vector fields, rather than general volume shadowing or density computation [S1, unofficial].
